# --- Hybrid search ---
pref-hybrid-title = Hybrid Search
pref-hybrid-desc = Keyword and semantic retrieval, each filtered against its own relevance threshold and then merged and ranked by rank fusion. The same four settings drive both library-wide search and digging into a single document.
pref-hybrid-gpu-label = GPU-Vektorbeschleunigung aktivieren
pref-hybrid-gpu-hint = Nur NVIDIA-Grafikkarten; ein kompatibler NVIDIA-Treiber ist erforderlich.
pref-hybrid-gpu-precision-label = Rechengenauigkeit
pref-hybrid-gpu-precision-hint = Auto verwendet Float32 bei ausreichendem GPU-Speicher, sonst Int8.
pref-hybrid-gpu-precision-auto = Auto
pref-hybrid-gpu-status-disabled = { $backend } · { $precision }; GPU-Beschleunigung ist ausgeschaltet.
pref-hybrid-gpu-status-preparing = GPU-Ressourcen werden vorbereitet...
pref-hybrid-gpu-status-loading = { $backend } · { $precision }; Vektoren werden geladen ({ $loaded }/{ $total })...
pref-hybrid-gpu-status-available = { $backend } · { $precision }; { $device }, { $vectors } Vektoren im Speicher.
pref-hybrid-gpu-status-synced = Synchronisiert um { $time }.
pref-hybrid-gpu-status-fallback = { $backend } · { $precision }; GPU nicht verfügbar ({ $code }): { $reason }
pref-hybrid-gpu-fallback-notification = GPU-Vektorbeschleunigung nicht verfügbar; CPU wird verwendet ({ $code }): { $reason }
pref-hybrid-retrieval-label = Retrieval limits
pref-hybrid-max-documents-label = Max highly relevant documents
pref-hybrid-max-documents-hint = How many documents one library-wide search may return. An upper bound only - weaker matches are never added to fill it.
pref-hybrid-max-chunks-label = Max chunks per document
pref-hybrid-max-chunks-hint = How many passages one document may return when the AI digs into it. Also an upper bound only.
pref-hybrid-fusion-explainer = The keyword branch and the semantic branch are judged separately, each on its own scale, and a document only has to clear ONE of the two thresholds to be kept — a branch can let a document in, but it can never keep one out. Whatever survives is then ordered by rank fusion: a document that placed well in both branches outranks one that placed well in only a single branch. These four settings apply to both hybrid_search (whole documents) and search_fulltext (passages inside one document).
pref-hybrid-keyword-min-score-label = Keyword relevance threshold
pref-hybrid-keyword-min-score-hint = How strong a keyword match has to be before the keyword branch keeps a document. Below this it contributes nothing — but the semantic branch can still bring the same document back on its own.
pref-hybrid-keyword-min-score-recommended = Recommended: 0.52 — measured, not guessed: 8 real queries scored against 931 documents from your own library, at the point that keeps the most genuinely relevant hits while dropping documents that merely happen to share one common word.
pref-hybrid-keyword-rrf-weight-label = Keyword RRF weight
pref-hybrid-keyword-rrf-weight-hint = How much a good keyword rank counts towards the final order. Raise it to trust exact terminology more; 0 turns the keyword branch off entirely. It does not change the threshold above — a down-weighted branch still keeps the same documents, they just count for less.
pref-hybrid-keyword-rrf-weight-recommended = Recommended: 1.0 — equal to the semantic weight. There is no evidence that either branch deserves to be trusted more on this library, so neither is favoured.
pref-hybrid-semantic-min-score-label = Semantic relevance threshold
pref-hybrid-semantic-min-score-hint = How close in meaning a document has to be before the semantic branch keeps it. Below this it contributes nothing — but a strong keyword match can still bring it back.
pref-hybrid-semantic-min-score-recommended = Recommended: 0.60 — the value this search has effectively been using all along, kept so results stay familiar.
pref-hybrid-semantic-rrf-weight-label = Semantic RRF weight
pref-hybrid-semantic-rrf-weight-hint = How much a good semantic rank counts towards the final order. Raise it to trust meaning over exact wording — useful when you often cannot name the right term; 0 turns the semantic branch off entirely.
pref-hybrid-semantic-rrf-weight-recommended = Recommended: 1.0 — equal to the keyword weight.
pref-hybrid-neighbor-radius-label = Neighbouring chunk expansion
pref-hybrid-neighbor-radius-hint = When a passage lacks context, how many passages either side the AI may pull in. 0 disables expansion.
pref-hybrid-advanced-title = Advanced: chunking (rebuild required)
pref-hybrid-chunk-target-label = Chunk target length
pref-hybrid-chunk-target-hint = How many characters of Markdown paragraphs each passage accumulates before it closes.
pref-hybrid-chunk-tolerance-label = Paragraph append tolerance
pref-hybrid-chunk-tolerance-hint = Once a passage reaches the target, a next paragraph no longer than this still joins it; a longer one starts the next passage.
pref-hybrid-chunk-stale-warning = Der vorhandene Index wurde mit anderen Chunk-Einstellungen erstellt als den untenstehenden. Bauen Sie den gesamten Index mit den Schaltflaechen oben neu auf - Vektoren und Stichwoerter zusammen.
pref-hybrid-vector-scan-timeout-label = Zeitlimit für Vektorscan (ms)
pref-hybrid-vector-scan-timeout-hint = Maximale Dauer des Indexscans im semantischen Zweig. Das Abfrage-Embedding hat ein eigenes Zeitlimit und verbraucht dieses Budget nicht.
pref-hybrid-keyword-search-timeout-label = Zeitlimit für Stichwortsuche (ms)
pref-hybrid-keyword-search-timeout-hint = Maximale Dauer der Suche in Zotero-Metadaten. Bei Überschreitung werden die bereits bewerteten Treffer zurückgegeben statt gar keiner.
pref-hybrid-scan-benchmark-button = Bibliotheksscan testen
pref-hybrid-scan-benchmark-hint = Misst beide Zweige an Ihrer echten Bibliothek und trägt für jedes Feld oben einen empfohlenen Wert ein. Sie können ihn danach weiterhin manuell ändern.
pref-hybrid-scan-benchmark-running-vector = Vektorscans werden ausgeführt...
pref-hybrid-scan-benchmark-running-keyword = Stichwortsuchen werden ausgeführt...
pref-hybrid-scan-benchmark-result-vector = Vektorscan ({ $runs } Durchläufe über { $chunks } Chunks) — kürzeste { $min } ms · Mittelwert { $average } ms · längste { $max } ms → empfohlen { $recommended } ms
pref-hybrid-scan-benchmark-result-keyword = Stichwortsuche ({ $runs } Durchläufe je Profil, langsamstes Profil „{ $profile }“) — kürzeste { $min } ms · Mittelwert { $average } ms · längste { $max } ms → empfohlen { $recommended } ms
pref-hybrid-scan-benchmark-result-profile =   · { $profile }: { $min } / { $average } / { $max } ms bei { $candidates } Kandidaten
pref-hybrid-scan-benchmark-coverage = Gemessen an { $chunks } indizierten Chunks und { $items } Stichproben. Wenn Sie später mehr indizieren, führen Sie den Test erneut aus — ein größerer Index scannt langsamer.
pref-hybrid-scan-benchmark-error = Scantest fehlgeschlagen: { $message }
pref-hybrid-scan-benchmark-col-item = Test
pref-hybrid-scan-benchmark-col-min = Kürzeste (ms)
pref-hybrid-scan-benchmark-col-average = Mittel (ms)
pref-hybrid-scan-benchmark-col-max = Längste (ms)
pref-hybrid-scan-benchmark-row-vector = Vektorscan
pref-hybrid-scan-benchmark-row-keyword = Stichwortsuche
